Searches Google and returns the first ten results, each with its title, URL, the snippet Google shows and the page's date when Google gives one. A snippet is Google's excerpt, which can be stale or cut off: enough to tell whether a subject exists and who writes about it, not to rely on for a fact. When Google can't be reached, Gemini searches Google instead and you get its written answer with its sources, which says less about each page. Search in the words the pages would use, and search again with other words rather than reading too much into one poor set of results.
